Article 3
The objectives of protection for women and children victims of acts of violence are to:
1. Prevent acts of violence against women and children, including trafficking in persons;
2. Eliminate all forms of violence and exploitation against women and children;
3. Protect and provide a sense of security for women and children victims of violence, complainants, and witnesses;
4. Provide services to women and children victims of acts of violence;
5. Facilitate and conduct mediation of cases of domestic violence to realize the integrity of a harmonious and prosperous household; and
6. Empowerment.

Article 7
The obligations and responsibilities of the Regional Government as referred to in Article 6 letter a, include:
a. establishing policies, programs, and activities for the protection of women and children from acts of violence;
b. conducting cooperation in the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence;
c. providing support for facilities and infrastructure for the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence; and
d. allocating a budget for the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence in accordance with regional financial capacity.
The duties of the Regional Government in the protection of women and children from acts of violence are as follows:
a. implementing policies for the protection of women and children from acts of violence established by the government;
b. collecting data and information about women and children in the context of efforts to protect them from acts of violence;
c. disseminating laws and regulations related to the prevention and protection of women and children from acts of violence; and
d. conducting monitoring and evaluation of the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence.

Article 8
The obligations and responsibilities of the community as referred to in Article 6 letter b, shall be implemented in the form of community participation.
The form of community participation as referred to in paragraph (1), includes:
1. preventing the occurrence of acts of violence against women and children;
2. providing protection to women and children from acts of violence, in the form of establishing rules of conduct in their respective areas starting from the Neighborhood Association level;
3. providing information and/or reporting acts of violence against women and children to law enforcement or authorized parties;
4. participating in the handling of victims of acts of violence; and
5. accompanying victims to service units.
The form of community participation as referred to in paragraph (2) shall be implemented responsibly in accordance with laws and regulations.

CHAPTER II
PRINCIPLES AND OBJECTIVES
Article 2
The Implementation and Protection of Women and Children victims of acts of violence is carried out based on the principles of: Humanity;
Respect for the rights of victims;
Justice and gender equality;
Protection;
Non-discrimination; and
The best interests of victims.

CHAPTER III
RIGHTS OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN
FROM ACTS OF VIOLENCE
Article 4
Women and children who are victims of acts of violence are entitled to the following rights:
1. The right to have their dignity and worth as human beings respected;
2. The right to health and psychological services for the suffering experienced by the victim;
3. The right to legal assistance;
4. The right to obtain information;
5. The right to confidential handling;
6. The right to social rehabilitation;
7. The right to handling of complaints;
8. The right of the victim and their family to obtain ease/facilitation in the judicial process; and
9. A guarantee of rights related to their status as members of the family and the community.

Article 11
Prevention of acts of violence against women and children as referred to in Article 10 shall be implemented by SKPD whose duties and functions are in the fields of:
social;
health;
education;
employment;
women's empowerment and child protection;
mental and spiritual; and
peace and order.
Prevention of acts of violence by SKPD as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented in an integrated and continuous manner.

CHAPTER VI
SERVICES FOR VICTIMS OF ACTS OF VIOLENCE
Article 12
(1) Forms of services provided to women and children victims of acts of violence are as follows:
    a. complaint services;
    b. medical services; and
    c. medicolegal services for the purposes of evidence in the field of law.
    d. legal aid services;
    e. independence or empowerment services; and
    f. social rehabilitation services.
(2) Forms of services as referred to in paragraph (1) are implemented by the relevant SKPD in accordance with the programs, activities, and budget available in each, in the fields of:
    a. social;
    b. health;
    c. women's empowerment and child protection;
    d. mental and spiritual;
    e. employment; and
    f. education.

Article 5
Child victims of acts of violence in addition to obtaining the rights as referred to in Article 4, also obtain special rights as follows: The right to survival, growth and development;
The right to basic service needs;
The right to equal protection; and The right to obtain freedom;

